WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:07.780
Multi-factor authentication means requiring more than one type of proof before granting access or completing a sensitive action.

2
00:00:07.880 --> 00:00:17.000
In a Python application, that proof may come from something the user knows, something the user has, or something unlocked locally on a trusted device.

3
00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:25.740
The exact method may change over time, but the purpose is stable: increase confidence that the person or entity using the account is legitimate.

4
00:00:26.020 --> 00:00:32.900
MFA is related to authentication, authorization, session management, and account recovery, but it does not replace them.

5
00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:35.480
Authentication verifies identity.

6
00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:37.820
MFA strengthens that verification.

7
00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:41.120
Authorization decides what the verified identity may do.

8
00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:45.460
Session management carries authenticated state after verification.

9
00:00:45.560 --> 00:00:49.640
Recovery gives users a way back into accounts when normal factors are unavailable.

10
00:00:49.740 --> 00:00:53.660
A weak recovery or session design can undermine even strong MFA.

11
00:00:53.940 --> 00:01:04.340
Python applications appear in many forms: Flask and Django sites, FastAPI services, internal tools, admin portals, APIs, and service platforms.

12
00:01:04.440 --> 00:01:10.440
In any of these contexts, MFA integration is more than adding a second screen after password login.

13
00:01:10.540 --> 00:01:21.180
The application must know when MFA is required, what state exists before MFA succeeds, how success upgrades the session, and how MFA events are logged and monitored.

14
00:01:21.460 --> 00:01:26.660
MFA improves assurance, but it does not make every request safe.

15
00:01:26.760 --> 00:01:36.280
A user who completes MFA still needs authorization checks before accessing records, changing settings, approving workflows, or using administrative features.

16
00:01:36.380 --> 00:01:43.820
MFA should connect to identity, sessions, risk, recovery, logging, monitoring, and user experience.

17
00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:50.560
The goal is stronger identity assurance without creating brittle custom flows or frustrating users unnecessarily.
